            There are three kinds of under-desk bike. A <strong>pedal exerciser</strong> is a
            small unit with pedals and a flywheel that sits on the floor in front of your own chair.
            A <strong>desk bike</strong> is a stationary bike with a built-in work surface. And a <strong>bike chair</strong> combines pedals with an office-style seat and back, to roll
            up to an ordinary desk. Most people should start with a pedal exerciser; desk bikes and
            bike chairs suit those who want a dedicated station. For gliding elliptical-motion
            pedallers such as the Cubii, see our guide to <a href="/best-under-desk-ellipticals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">under-desk ellipticals</a>.
          </p>
